    {
      "id": 35,
      "title": "Event and counter coverage",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 144,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "These panels keep **exported log records**, **native counter increases** and the **deduplicated rollout census** separate. Missing data is not zero use.\n\n**MCP:** result records describe the exported stream. **RTK:** a request-prefix marker cannot prove a hook rewrite. **Codex hooks:** diagnostic log records are partial; the native completion metric supplies the counter estimate, with lifecycle/status labels after Collector retention is applied. **Claude hooks:** sum the native numeric outcomes because one completion log covers multiple matching commands. Lifecycle labels do not identify each RTK or ai-memory processor.\n\n**Confirmed RTK rewrite totals and per-processor hook firings remain unmeasured here.** Approval-decision source is Config, User or AutomatedReviewer. Do not sum these panels into tool usage, token savings or the historical census."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 36,
      "title": "Claude native hook outcomes (range)",
      "description": "Sums the native hook_execution_complete fields num_success, num_blocking, num_non_blocking_error and num_cancelled. One completion log covers all matching hook commands, so its record count is not the command count. hook_event is the lifecycle; raw matcher and script identities are not exposed. Requires native hook event export and the reviewed numeric-field retention; absent observations do not mean zero firings.",
      "type": "bargauge",
      "datasource": {
        "uid": "ns2604-loki"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 136,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
